// as a single 8-wide row and the same formula still reads it, so no state
// needs a special case.
//
// ONE `cell` AND ONE FOOT ANCHOR PER CHARACTER, unlike GUARD_ART's per-state
// pairs. The guards needed per-state anchors because their states were packed
// corner-aligned at different canvas sizes; here every frame is pasted CENTRED
// in the cell, and the source canvases are concentric (a bigger canvas holds
// the same body at the same size with symmetric padding), so all states share
// one alignment. `cell` is the largest canvas the character ships anywhere;
// `footX`/`footY` are the anchor to draw it at -- footX is the cell centre,
// footY the measured lowest opaque row of the IDLE sheet, i.e. where the
// character's feet stand in the pose the player sees most. Each state also
// carries its own measured `foot` for anyone who needs it.
//
// `frameMs` is DERIVED, not shipped: these exports carry no timing data at
// all. Walks are paced to a 720ms full cycle (round 24's
