// round 3) so a 6-frame and an 8-frame walk cover a stride in the same time.
// Attacks are paced to 420ms, WorldScene's MONSTER_ATTACK_SECONDS.
//
// THE PACKS ARE NOT UNIFORM -- branch on `animKeys`, never assume:
//   * robcollins and pirateM ship NO attack (walk only).
//   * pirateQueen ships no attack either; instead it has `stance`, a looping
//     cutlass-drawn idle. It is an idle, not a swing -- checked frame by
//     frame -- so it is not passed off as an attack.
//   * everyone else has idle + walk + attack.
// `mirroredDirs` lists any direction whose frames were synthesised by
// horizontally flipping the mirror-image direction, because the export was
// short: the wraith's run shipped only five of eight directions.
//
// NO PALETTE VARIANTS FOR PEOPLE. Every earlier humanoid round shipped soft
// recolors (NPC_ART's `_v1`/`_v2`) so one sprite could stand in for several
// townsfolk. These are named individuals with dialogue, so a recolour would
// be a different person, not more variety. The castle wall repeats along a
// rampart, so it alone carries the two soft variants, at round 45's bounds.

